{"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L83","fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/track"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first, each with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, as "},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds it; the record’s own "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0\""},{"type":"text","text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no other device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing, rather than an event with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which Mixpanel would attribute to no user,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events of the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" as one, so a recovered record that Mixpanel had already stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The record’s vendor identifier and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version and build, each left out when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name and version","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" Mixpanel takes, and one too large for Mixpanel ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. Mixpanel answers a request it reads with 200, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" retries one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"413. Mixpanel answers 200 as well when it ingests none of a request’s events: a wrong region,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored, so check the project’s Live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"View after setting it up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days: a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"older than that when it is sent, such as one a store kept through a long time offline, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted as delivered and not stored. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The bytes are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"]}],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"title":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code"